I think we often see leadership  development as self development there's  the individual level that's where we're  really thinking about you as a person  you know a good leader understands what  she has to do to make herself develop  but there's a second level that's the  organizational level a great leader  understands and does what she has to do  to help others to develop most leaders  are not running entire companies most  leaders are touching only a handful of  people maybe they don't have any formal  leadership authority but they do touch  their peers and their colleagues at work  and those interactions are opportunities  to show leadership all of us are  challenged to engage in behaviors that  essentially have leadership implications  for the people around us how do your  actions as a leader affect the growth  mindset of others and then finally the  third level of analysis is the  environment of the organization this  includes society economy the broader  culture the natural environment the  things each of us do at work not only  matter for work they also matter for the  broader world because our actions as  leaders in order for us to be  exceptional also will have implications  at that third level transform your  approach to leadership excellence and  development learn more about SCP the  Stanford executive program  [Music]
 

